UPDATE companies SET description='Dangar Engineering & Mfg. has operated from Ventura, California since its founding in 1954. The company was established with a focus on mastering the edge of machining technology, choosing to specialize in the difficult and unusual parts that other shops could not produce.

The shop provides large precision CNC machining, including 5-axis milling of complex parts, tooling, prototypes, and production runs. Its equipment includes 5-axis machines with a 242-inch by 115-inch by 25-inch machining envelope (part envelope up to 242 by 115 by 72 inches) and a coordinate measuring machine with a 161.75 by 54 by 53.375-inch inspection envelope, all housed in a 24-hour temperature-controlled facility. Design and NC programming are performed using CATIA CAD/CAM. The company employs 50 to 99 people and also offers inspection, reverse engineering, complex assemblies, welding, and fabrication.

Dangar serves aerospace, architectural, automotive, commercial, medical, and marine industries. Its customer approvals include Northrop Grumman, Lockheed Martin, Litton, Volvo, BMW, Volkswagen, and Pilkington Aerospace. Machined parts are used in commercial and military aerospace applications as well as titanium components implanted in the human body.

The company''s stated philosophy is to be a reliable source of high-precision, close-tolerance products with exceptional quality, positioning itself as a one-stop shop for any-angle 5-axis holes and very complex geometry.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["5-axis CNC machining", "Large precision CNC machining", "CNC milling", "Tooling", "Production machining", "Prototyping", "CMM inspection", "Reverse engineering", "Quality inspection", "Complex assemblies", "Welding", "Fabrication", "CATIA CAD/CAM programming", "Design services"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Architectural", "Automotive", "Commercial", "Medical", "Marine"], "materials": ["Titanium"], "equipment": ["5-axis CNC machines (242\" x 115\" x 25\" envelope)", "CMM (161.75\" x 54\" x 53.375\" envelope)", "CATIA CAD/CAM software", "24-hour temperature-controlled facility"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Specializes in difficult, complex, and unusual precision parts", "5-axis CNC machining with 242\" x 115\" x 72\" part envelope", "24-hour temperature-controlled manufacturing and inspection facility", "CATIA CAD/CAM design and NC programming", "Approved supplier to major aerospace and automotive OEMs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1954 -> db", "Headquarters Ventura, California -> db", "Employee count 50-99 -> db", "Specializes in large precision CNC machining, 5-axis milling -> /", "5-axis machining envelope 242\" x 115\" x 25\" (machine) and 242\" x 115\" x 72\" (part) -> /", "CMM inspection envelope 161.75\" x 54\" x 53.375\" -> /", "24-hour temperature-controlled facility -> /", "CATIA CAD/CAM design and NC programming -> /", "Services: tooling, production, prototypes, inspection, reverse engineering, complex assemblies, welding & fabrication -> /", "Industries: Aerospace, Architectural, Automotive, Commercial, Medical, Marine -> /", "Customer approvals: Northrop Grumman, Lockheed Martin, Litton, Volvo, BMW, Volkswagen, Pilkington Aerospace -> /", "Ti