UPDATE companies SET description='Darn It! Inc. operates from New Bedford, Massachusetts, where it was established in 1996 by Jeff Glassman. Glassman launched the business after his family’s apparel factory lost the majority of its workforce to lower-cost competitors in Mexico; a former customer asked him to repair 30,000 damaged trousers, prompting the creation of a company focused on refurbishing clothing. The firm remains family-run.

The company provides warehousing, distribution, and refurbishment services. Its quality-control offerings include 100% inspection of soft lines and hard goods, labeling, sewing repairs, button and snap replacement, cleaning (with an ozone room for odor removal), laundering, mold remediation, pressing, packaging, kitting, and reverse logistics such as returns processing and restocking. The warehouse and distribution arm accounts for roughly 40 percent of revenue and serves more than 20 clients, handling merchandise that ranges from apparel to books and watches.

Customers include retailers, manufacturers, wholesalers, and web-based businesses worldwide. In one case, Darn It! corrected 1,200 mislabeled shirts for a retailer; in another, it inspected 8,000 sets of blackout curtains, recovering 91 percent as sellable inventory through inspection, sewing repairs, and spot cleaning.

Glassman started the business to fill a gap in repairing damaged goods from overseas production, and the company emphasizes quick turnaround to support lean inventory programs for its clients.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["100% Quality Inspection", "Inspection of Soft Lines and Hard Goods", "Product Defect Inspection", "Labeling (Main/Care Label Printing/Replacement, Bar Coding, Heat Transfer Labeling, Heat Transfer Removal)", "Sewing Repairs and Alterations", "Button/Snap/Rivet Replacement", "Trimming and Part Replacement", "Ozone Room Odor Removal", "Laundering and Spot Cleaning", "Mold and Mildew Removal", "Garment Pressing and Steaming", "Kitting, Sorting, and Counting", "Hang Tag/Price Ticket Changes", "Re-bagging (Boxed or Hanging)", "Re-boxing", "Re-labeling", "Reverse Logistics (Receive, Record, Report Returns)", "Restockable vs Damaged Sorting", "Repair to A-Stock Quality", "Project-Specific Returns Processing", "Long-Term Returns Processing", "Warehousing and Distribution", "Inventory Management", "Door-to-Door Logistics"], "industries": ["Retail", "Manufacturing", "Wholesale", "E-commerce"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Ozone Room"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Door-to-door logistic solutions and warehousing", "100% inspection and refurbishment for soft lines and hard goods", "Ozone room for odor removal and mold remediation", "Reverse logistics and returns processing", "Family-owned since 1996"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 in New Bedford, MA -> /about-us", "Family-run distribution and refurbishment business -> /about-us", "Jeff Glassman founder, launched after factory lost business to Mexico -> /about-us", "Warehouse/distribution arm 40% revenue, >20 customers -> /about-us", "Services: 100% inspection, labeling, sewing repairs, cleaning, ozone room, packaging, reverse logistics -> /quality", "Industries: retailers, manufacturers, wholesalers, web-based businesses -> /about-us", "Case