UPDATE companies SET description='Delicious New Mexico operates from Albuquerque in Bernalillo County, New Mexico. The initiative was developed through the Hispanic-American Institute under a USDA/AMS grant and is a program of the Rio Grande Community Development Corporation, a 501(c)(3) tax-exempt organization. While a precise founding year is not published, the team notes nearly 20 years of experience working with food businesses across the state.

The organization runs a fleet of refrigerated vehicles on weekly statewide routes, picking up from multiple farms on a single trip to consolidate loads and reduce costs. Services include scheduled pick-up and delivery for a flat fee, assistance with wholesale packaging and pricing, and retail placement coordination. Three staff members are listed as contacts: a director of finance and programs, a facilities manager, and a project coordinator.

Delicious New Mexico serves small and mid-sized farms, food producers, and retail outlets throughout New Mexico. Customers include Legacy Acres Farm in Tucumcari, which moved 100 pounds of cabbage to Meals on Wheels; Dulce Tradición, which placed biscuits in retail stores; and the Agri-cultura Network, a collective of farms that pools products for processing and distribution in Bernalillo County.

The initiative was created because transporting produce during planting and harvest seasons pulls farmers away from core work, incurs fuel and vehicle expenses, and often requires multiple trips or half-full trucks. By consolidating shipments and providing daily refrigerated transport, Delicious New Mexico aims to save producers time and money while strengthening local food distribution.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Refrigerated food transportation", "Multi-farm consolidated pickup", "Statewide distribution routing", "Flat-fee delivery scheduling", "Wholesale packaging and pricing assistance", "Retail placement coordination", "Order pooling and distribution efficiency"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Food production", "Food distribution", "Retail food", "Local food systems"], "materials": ["Fresh produce", "Shelf-stable food products", "Value-added food products"], "equipment": ["Refrigerated vehicles (fleet)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Consolidated multi-farm pickup on single trips to lower transportation costs", "Weekly statewide routes operated with a fleet of refrigerated vehicles", "Flat-fee pricing for pick-up and delivery", "Bilingual customer service (English and Spanish)", "Non-profit structure focused on local food system development"], "facts_used": ["Location: Albuquerque, Bernalillo County, New Mexico -> /", "Ownership: Initiative of Rio Grande Community Development Corporation (501(c)(3)) -> /", "Founding context: Developed through Hispanic-American Institute under USDA/AMS grant -> /", "Experience: Nearly 20 years working with food businesses -> /", "Services: Refrigerated transportation, multi-farm pickup, statewide weekly routes, flat-fee pricing -> /", "Staff: Briana Smith (Director of Finance + Programs), Louis (DMAC Facilities Manager), Bryan Diaz (Project Coordinator) -> /", "Customers: Legacy Acres Farm, Dulce Tradici\u00f3n, Agri-cultura Network -> /", "Languages: English 