UPDATE companies SET description='Dravon Medical Inc. operates from Clackamas, Oregon, where it was founded in 1974. The company has spent over five decades as a medical device manufacturer and contract manufacturing partner for original equipment manufacturers (OEMs).

The company produces disposable medical tubing clamps — including the True Blue A-Clamp for fluid occlusion and the T-Clamp for securing towels, drapes, and sponges — as well as custom medical fluid and IV bags manufactured via radio frequency (RF) welding and heat sealing. Its FDA-registered, ISO 13485:2016 certified facility includes two ISO Class 7 cleanrooms dedicated to RF welding, heat sealing, assembly, and packaging. Dravon supports projects from prototype tooling through full-scale production, offering design-for-manufacturing guidance and small-volume flexibility.

Dravon serves medical device OEMs and healthcare professionals across dialysis, blood collection, blood banking, fluid management, and clinical or surgical environments. Its clamps and bags are used in applications ranging from dialysis and blood collection to surgical draping, while its contract manufacturing services support OEMs needing cleanroom assembly, packaging, and regulatory-compliant production.

The company emphasizes its quality management system built on repeatability, traceability, validation, and regulatory compliance. It highlights decades of expertise in RF-welded thermoplastic bags (including PVC, non-DEHP, and PVC-free films), responsive engineering support, and long-term OEM partnerships as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','FDA Registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["RF welding of thermoplastic medical fluid bags", "Heat sealing", "Cleanroom assembly (ISO Class 7)", "Cleanroom packaging (ISO Class 7)", "Custom medical fluid/IV bag manufacturing", "Disposable medical tubing clamp manufacturing (A-Clamps, T-Clamps)", "Tooling for prototypes", "Design for manufacturing (DFM) support", "Contract manufacturing for medical device OEMs", "Small-volume production flexibility"], "industries": ["Medical device manufacturing", "Healthcare", "Dialysis", "Blood collection", "Blood banking", "Fluid management", "Clinical and surgical environments"], "materials": ["PVC", "Non-DEHP materials", "PVC-free materials", "Reinforced nylon", "Aluminum (X-ray visible rivet)"], "equipment": ["RF welding equipment", "Heat sealing equipment", "Two ISO Class 7 cleanrooms"], "volume": "Prototype to full-scale production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Prototype through production support", "Responsive engineering and design-for-manufacturing guidance", "Two ISO Class 7 cleanrooms for RF welding, heat sealing, assembly, and packaging", "FDA registered and ISO 13485:2016 certified quality system", "Decades of experience with RF-welded medical fluid bags and disposable clamps"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Clackamas, Oregon -> db", "Founded: 1974 -> /", "Products: disposable medical tubing clamps (A-Clamps, T-Clamps), custom medical fluid/IV bags -> /", "Processes: RF welding, heat sealing, cleanroom assembly, packaging, tooling for prototypes -> /", "Facility: FDA registered, ISO 13485:2016 certified, two ISO Class 7 cle