UPDATE companies SET description='EDCOR Electronics Corporation operates from Carlsbad, New Mexico, where it has been based since January 1991. The company traces its roots to the early 1960s in Utah, where it began as Electronic Development Corporation, a public firm that pioneered wireless microphones and held the first U.S. patent in that field. After several ownership changes and relocations — through Costa Mesa, Irvine, and Santa Ana, California — the management team bought out all shareholders in late 1990, financed the move to New Mexico, and reincorporated the business there.

The company designs and manufactures a broad line of transformers and related components. Its catalog includes audio matching transformers (microphone, line level, combiners, splitters), audio distribution transformers, stereo-to-mono couplers, classic tube audio transformers (single-ended, push-pull, interstage), power transformers for tube and solid-state equipment, chokes and inductors (DC power chokes, high-voltage plate/filament), and a range of parts such as coil bobbins (nylon 6/6 glass-filled), steel laminations, end bells, brackets, and mounting hardware. EDCOR also offers custom transformer design and sells amplifier replacement transformers and kit transformers for brands such as Fender, Dynaco, and Decware.

EDCOR serves professional audio installers, musicians, amplifier builders, and hobbyists. Its distribution transformers were used in the refit of the Rose Bowl in the mid-to-late 1980s. Current customers include tube amplifier designers like Pete Millett and Bruce Heran (OddWatt), kit builders (Decware ZEN kits), and repair shops needing replacements for vintage Fender, Dynaco, and other amplifiers. The company also supports the DIY community with technical blogs and design resources.

EDCOR emphasizes domestic manufacturing: "Proudly designed and built in ''MERICA," with a stated effort to source materials and parts from U.S. suppliers. The transformer production process has evolved over four decades, originally driven by the company''s own difficulty in obtaining quality audio and power transformers in the early 1980s, which led to the acquisition of Delta Magnetics and its manufacturing facilities.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Audio matching transformer manufacturing", "Audio distribution transformer manufacturing", "Stereo to mono coupling transformer manufacturing", "Classic tube audio transformer manufacturing (single-ended, push-pull, interstage)", "Power transformer manufacturing (tube and solid-state)", "Choke/inductor manufacturing (DC power chokes, high-voltage plate/filament)", "Custom transformer design", "Coil bobbin molding (nylon 6/6 glass-filled)", "Steel lamination processing", "Transformer hardware fabrication (end bells, brackets, channels/frames, mounting insulators/pads)", "Amplifier kit transformer supply", "Transformer replacement for vintage amplifiers (Fender, Dynaco, etc.)"], "industries": ["Professional audio / commercial sound", "Musical instrument amplification", "Audio installation / contracting", "DIY / hobbyist audio", "Vintage amplifier restoration"], "materials": ["Steel laminations", "Nylon 6/6 glass-filled (bobbins)", "Magnet wire (implied)", "Core materials (various)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proudly designed and built in the USA with domestic material sourcing", "Custom transformer design service", "Over four decades of transformer production process development", "Direct sales and technical support via email and phone"], "facts_used": ["HQ Carlsbad, NM -> db", "Founded early 1960s Utah as Electronic Development Corp -> /about-us", "Management buyout 1990, move to NM 1991 -> /about-us", "Product lines: audio matching, distribution, tube, power, chokes, parts -> / and /about-us", "Custom design service -> /", "Rose Bowl refit 1980s -> /about-us", "Customers: Pete Millett, Bruce Heran, Decware, Fender, Dynaco -> / and /about-us", "Domestic manufacturing claim -> /", "Acquired Delta Magnetics 1982 -> /about-us", "Materials: steel laminations, nylon 6/6 glass-filled -> /", "Hours M-Th 7-3:30 MST -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "EDCOR acquired Delta Magnetics and manufacturing facilities and started producing their own transformers.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='edcor-electronics-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='EEI Manufacturing Services, now operating as Impact ES–Clearwater, is based in Clearwater, Florida. The business traces its roots to the Pacific Northwest through its parent company, Impact Electronic Solutions, which is headquartered in Lake Oswego, Oregon. EEI brought over 25 years of leadership in advanced PCB assembly technology before the subsidiary brands were unified under the Impact Electronic Solutions name in a recent reorganization. The transition was described as a visual and organizational change only, with all service levels, contacts, and operations remaining consistent.

Impact ES–Clearwater provides full-service electronics design and manufacturing, centered on advanced PCB assembly. Its capabilities span value-added engineering services, prototype and full-turnkey production, troubleshooting, and bottom-up design. The company operates as part of a multisite network of full-service design and manufacturing facilities that also includes locations in Cranston, Rhode Island; Grants Pass, Oregon; Vancouver, Washington; and Ventura, California.

The facility serves aerospace, defense, homeland security, military and defense, space, autonomous and robotics, commercial and industrial, and medical and life sciences sectors. Customers include industry leaders in these fields who require robust turnkey solutions and advanced manufacturing to meet demands for agility and quality, including alignment with the Defense Department''s Better Buying Power affordability initiative.

The company states its vision is to be the most and agile supplier of advanced, cost-effective electronics manufacturing for customers supporting national defense and security. It emphasizes being an extension of the customer''s organization, with a focus on service, quality, and innovation as the reasons customers return.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB Assembly", "Electronics design and manufacturing", "Value-added engineering services", "Prototype production", "Full-turnkey production", "End-to-end aerospace manufacturing", "Troubleshooting", "Bottom-up design"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Homeland Security", "Medical & Life Sciences", "Military & Defense", "Space", "Autonomous & Robotics", "Commercial & Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 25 years of leadership in advanced PCB assembly technology", "Multisite network of full-service design and manufacturing facilities across the United States", "All legacy EEI certifications retained and expanded under Impact Electronic Solutions", "Service levels, contacts, and operations unchanged through brand transition"], "facts_used": ["Location: Clearwater, FL -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label) and page ''/'' (locations list)", "Parent company: Impact Electronic Solutions, HQ Lake Oswego, OR -> page ''/''", "Over 25 years leadership in PCB assembly -> page ''/''", "Brand unification under Impact Electronic Solutions -> page ''/''", "Services: PCB assembly, design, engineering, prototype, turnkey, troubleshooting, bottom-up design -> page ''/''", "Facilities: Clearwater, Cranston, Grants Pass, Vancouver, Ventura -> page ''/''", "Industries served: aerospace, defense, homeland security, medical, military, space, autonomous/robotics, commercial/industrial -> page ''/''", "Certifications retained and expanded -> page ''/''", "Vision: trusted agile supplier for defense/security -> page ''/''", "Service levels unchanged through transition -> page ''/''"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "provide customers with over 25 years of leadership and experience in advanced PCB Assembly technology... full-service electronics design and manufacturing services", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='eei-manufacturing-services' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='EIC Semiconductor Inc is headquartered in Irwindale, California. The company operates as a manufacturer of discrete semiconductor devices.

EIC provides end-to-end manufacturing with a dedicated wafer fabrication facility and assembly plant, allowing control over quality and supply. The company produces a broad portfolio of discrete semiconductors, including Zener diodes, switching diodes, rectifier diodes, transient voltage suppressors (TVS), thyristors, and small-signal transistors. Its catalog encompasses over 15,000 part numbers across more than 50 package types. TVS devices range from 150 W to 50,000 W, while silicon rectifier diodes offer avalanche voltages up to 2,500 V and reverse voltages up to 3,000 V, with AEC-Q101 qualification. High-voltage ultra-fast recovery rectifiers are available with reverse voltages from 7,500 V to 12,000 V.

The company serves automotive electronics, automotive rectifier diodes, aviation, medical, power supply, industrial electronics, and consumer electronics markets.

