UPDATE companies SET description='Elite Medical Supplies, LLC operates from Laramie, Wyoming, with a second location in Casper. The company’s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The firm distributes a broad range of medical, industrial, and scientific supplies. Its product catalog includes mobility aids such as walkers, rollators, canes, and crutches; bath aids including commodes, shower chairs, and grab bars; bedroom equipment like home hospital beds and pressure mattresses; incontinence products; catheter supplies; and wound care items. The company also offers rental and bulk purchase options for facilities and individuals.

Elite Medical Supplies serves healthcare providers, industrial clients, and scientific institutions. It bills Medicare, Medicaid, and Blue Cross Blue Shield directly, and works with other insurance carriers.

The company emphasizes competitive pricing, stating it offers top-quality products at lower prices than other suppliers. It highlights reliable customer service, noting that its team works in the healthcare industry and advocates for customers when adjusting its product catalog. Fast delivery and everyday low prices are cited as core commitments.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Medical supply distribution", "Healthcare, industrial, and scientific equipment supply", "Insurance billing (Medicare, Medicaid, Blue Cross Blue Shield)", "Rental and bulk purchase programs", "Showroom and direct sales", "Customer product selection assistance"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Industrial", "Scientific"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Laramie, Wyoming -> db", "Additional location in Casper, Wyoming -> /", "Product categories: mobility, bath aids, bedroom, incontinence, catheters, wound care -> /", "Insurance billing: Medicare, Medicaid, Blue Cross Blue Shield -> /", "Showroom access in Laramie and Casper -> /", "Rental and bulk purchase options -> /", "Competitive pricing claim -> /", "Customer service emphasis and advocacy -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We offer a vast amount of Healthcare, Industrial, and Scientific supplies and equipment.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='elite-medical-supplies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='EMSI – Electrostim Medical Services, Inc. is a privately held medical device company headquartered in Tampa, Florida. The business was founded in 1995 by Mario Garcia, Jr., who serves as chairman and founder. Garcia, a Tampa native, established the company as a start-up and has since grown it into a national operation.

The company specializes in home electrical stimulation devices, bracing, and accessories for pain management and physical rehabilitation. EMSI reports serving over 70,000 patients and employs approximately 400 people across its operations. Its services include billing, patient support, customer service, Medicare processing, and accounts receivable management.

EMSI emphasizes its accreditations as differentiators: it is Joint Commission accredited, a member of ADMEA, recognized by Cigna Healthy Workforce, and its devices are FDA approved. The founder’s original aim was to build a national medical device company focused on efficient, professional service that increases client profitability.', certifications=ARRAY['FDA Approved','Joint Commission Accredited','ADMEA Member','Cigna Healthy Workforce']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrotherapy device manufacturing", "Bracing fabrication", "Medical device distribution", "Patient billing services", "Medicare claims processing", "Customer support services", "Patient support services", "Accounts receivable management"], "industries": ["Pain management", "Physical rehabilitation", "Home healthcare", "Medical devices", "Durable medical equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Specializes in home electrical stimulation devices, bracing, and accessories", "Joint Commission accredited", "FDA approved devices", "Services over 70,000 patients nationally", "Approximately 400 employees"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Tampa, Florida -> /about", "Founded in 1995 by Mario Garcia, Jr. -> /about", "Privately held company -> /about", "Specializes in home electrical stimulation devices, bracing, and accessories -> /about", "Services over 70,000 patients -> /about", "Employs approximately 400 people -> /about", "Joint Commission Accredited -> /", "Member of ADMEA -> /", "Cigna Healthy Workforce -> /", "FDA Approved -> / and db", "Total Medical Resources division supplies medical products -> /", "Operations include Billing, Patient Support Services, Customer Service, Medicare, Accounts Receivable -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a medical device company specializing in home electrical stimulation devices, bracing, and accessories for pain management and ph