UPDATE companies SET description='East Penn Manufacturing, a private, family-owned company, was founded in 1946 by Air Force veteran DeLight Breidegam Jr. and his father, DeLight Sr., in a one-room creamery in Bowers, Pennsylvania. The business began by rebuilding used batteries to meet post-war demand from returning GIs. In 1947, Karl Gasche joined as a partner, and the Deka brand—derived from "DeLight" and "Karl"—was born. Today the company operates a major battery finishing and distribution plant in Temple, Texas, alongside what it describes as the world''s largest single-site lead battery manufacturing facility.

East Penn produces lead-acid batteries for automotive, industrial, motive power, transportation, and reserve power (UPS, telecommunications, renewable energy) applications. Its product portfolio spans 515 designs, supported by vertically integrated operations that include wire and cable manufacturing, battery accessories, and custom solutions. The company reports over 10,500 full-time employees worldwide and operates through divisions such as Motive Power, Transportation, Reserve Power, and Wire & Cable, as well as subsidiaries including Navitas Systems (lithium technology), MK Battery, East Penn Canada, and East Penn International.

Customers span automotive OEMs, material-handling equipment makers, commercial truck fleets, telecommunications providers, and renewable-energy integrators. The company has been recognized by Honda and John Deere for supplier sustainability, and its batteries serve applications ranging from lift trucks and commercial vehicles to critical backup power for data centers and outside plant.

The founding principle of putting customers and employees first remains central, reinforced by an integrated quality and environmental management system. East Penn emphasizes pollution prevention, waste reduction, and compliance with global standards, holding multiple internationally recognized certifications. A $110 million expansion announced for the Texas facility in 2026 underscores continued investment in domestic capacity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Lead-acid battery manufacturing", "Battery finishing", "Distribution", "Wire and cable manufacturing", "Battery accessory production", "Custom battery solutions", "Motive power battery production", "Transportation battery production", "Reserve power battery production", "Lithium battery systems (via Navitas Systems)"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Industrial", "Commercial", "Backup power/UPS", "Material handling", "Transportation", "Telecommunications", "Renewable energy", "Motive power", "Reserve power"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest single-site lead battery manufacturing facility in the world", "Family-owned since 1946 with veteran founder", "Over 10,500 employees and 515 product designs", "Vertically integrated with lithium subsidiary (Navitas Systems) and specialty brands", "Recognized by Honda and John Deere for sustainability"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1946 in Bowers, PA by DeLight Breidegam Jr. and DeLight Sr. -> /about", "Private, family-owned company operating largest single-site lead battery manufacturing facility -> /", "Over 10,500 full-time employees, 515 product designs -> /about", "Operates battery finishing and distribution plant in Temple, Texas -> db", "$110 million investment announced in 2026 -> db", "Divisions: Motive Power, Transportation, Reserve Power, Wire & Cable -> /", "Subsidiaries: East Penn Canada, East Penn International, Navitas Systems, MK Battery -> /", "Recognized by 